# Google Drive sync configuration.
#
# Trading Journal stores all journal data (trades, strategies, instruments,
# chart exercises, settings, profile, syllabus progress) as CSV files in a
# "TradingJournal" folder in the signed-in user's Google Drive. There is no
# local storage fallback, so this must be configured for the app to work.
#
# To create a Client ID:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick) a project.
#   2. Enable the "Google Drive API" for that project.
#   3. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External is fine for personal use;
#      add your own Google account as a test user if the app stays "Testing").
#   4. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Web application".
#   5. Add every origin you'll load the app from under
#      "Authorized JavaScript origins", e.g.:
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://your-deployed-domain.example
#   6. Copy the generated Client ID below.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
